<title>SPAIN: Spain Q2 average earnings up 4.6 pct year on year.</title>
<headline>Spain Q2 average earnings up 4.6 pct year on year.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish average earnings per worker per month rose 4.6 percent year on year in the second quarter, the National Statistics Institute INE said on Thursday.</p>
<p>In the first quarter average monthly earnings rose 4.3 percent year on year.</p>
<p>Earnings were on average 198,648 pesetas per month in the second quarter.</p>
<p>A breakdown of the data showed that wages rose 5.8 percent year on year in the industrial sector in the second quarter, by 4.8 percent in construction and by 3.2 percent in the services sector.</p>
<p>-- Madrid newsroom +341 585 2160</p>
</text>
